# The vowel the module did not have, and the chain that reaches it.
#
# Central Catalan has a schwa and Castilian has not. It is not a refinement:
# every unstressed a and e in the language is one, so it is the commonest
# vowel in any Catalan sentence and the single thing that makes the language
# sound like itself rather than like Spanish.
#
# A phoneme code that has never existed is invisible to every rule that asks
# what its neighbours are, and the one that matters here is stanspan_vals: it
# is a chain of alternatives testing the phone against each vowel in turn, and
# a code with no arm falls straight past every one of them into the tail with
# no formants set at all, so the vowel comes out as whatever the phone before
# it left behind. So the chain is written again with an arm for the schwa in
# it.
#
# What is kept from IBM's is everything else, in the same order: the fence,
# the seven vowels it already had, the breathiness a female voice wants, the
# nasalisation of a vowel beside a nasal, and insert_acoustic_vals, which is
# what reads the formants the arm just set. Only the schwa arm is new.

# The block IBM's own rule runs before nasalize_vow, kept exactly as it was.
# It is raw lower notation inside a bare rule because what it does cannot be
# said in the upper form: it hands if_testeq_v_i the address of a state cell,
# and the notation has a word for a state variable's value and none for where
# it lives. A bare rule owns its registers, so a copy of IBM's own lines is
# safe here in a way it would not be inside a rule the compiler is allocating.
rule cat_fem_breathiness takes 1 from ss_ssval.obj
  bare
  raw load movl slot 8 into r6
  raw push reg r6
  raw call ZZstarttest15 arity 1 depth 1
  raw push imm 1
  raw addk 3024 reg r6 into r3
  raw push reg r3
  raw addk 3026 reg r6 into r7
  raw push reg r6
  raw store movw imm 4 ind reg r7 0
  raw call if_testeq_v_i arity 3 depth 4
  raw popn 4
  if answer is 0
    raw push imm 100
    raw push reg r3
    raw push reg r6
    raw store movw imm 6 ind reg r7 0
    raw call if_testneq_v_i arity 3 depth 3
    raw popn 3
    if answer is 0
      call ZZstarttest15
      call modify_breathiness_for_femV
    end
  end
  answer 0
end

# Whether the phone the chain is looking at carries no stress. The phone
# statement has a stress field -- offset 8, two bytes -- that
# copy_stress_to_phones fills in from the syllable structure, so by the time
# the value chain runs it says which vowels the word leans on. Nothing in
# IBM's Spanish ever asks, because Spanish reduces nothing.
rule cat_unstressed takes 1 from ss_ssval.obj
  bare
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  call testFldeq 4 8 0
end

# What the schwa sounds like. A vowel rule is five numbers -- the first
# formant once and the second and third twice each, because the transition
# into a vowel and the one out of it are separate targets -- and several
# hundred lines of context tests that move them for the consonants around.
# This is the five. Spanish's own a is 660, 1400 and 2450 and its e is 480,
# 1800 and 2650, and the schwa sits between them and further in: mid, central,
# and the mouth nearer to rest than for either.
#
# It needs no amplitude of its own, and the two below do, for the reason their
# comment gives: the schwa is never a phone code at all. Nothing lays code 37
# down -- the reduction happens here, on the a or the e the letter rules
# already wrote -- so every rule downstream still sees a vowel Spanish knows.
rule cat_ph_schwa_vals takes 1 from ss_ssval.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2930 to 600
  set global half 2938 to 1500
  set global half 2942 to 1500
  set global half 2946 to 2450
  set global half 2950 to 2450
  match
end

# The open e and the open o, which Catalan has and Castilian has not. They
# are the vowels of sec, dona and cafe with a grave, and they differ from the
# close pair mostly in the first formant: the mouth is further open, which is
# what open means. Castilian's e is 480, 1800 and 2650 and its o 480, 900 and
# 2500, so these sit below both.
#
# Six numbers rather than five, and the sixth is why cafe with a grave came
# out as a hole. These two are real phone codes -- 38 and 39, laid down by
# apply_span_enye_rules -- and the value chain is not the only chain that asks
# a phone which vowel it is. get_stanspan_nuc_AV is another: it sets the
# amplitude of voicing at offset 2722 from an arm apiece for i, e, a, o and u,
# and a code with no arm leaves the field alone, so the open vowels were
# spoken at whatever amplitude the consonant before them had left there. After
# a d or a p that is silence, which is what a listener reported: nearly a
# fifth of a sentence full of graves was not voiced at all.
#
# So they set it themselves. That the chain writes nothing for them is what
# makes this sound rather than a race: get_stanspan_nuc_AV runs after this
# rule, from inside insert_acoustic_vals, and for these two codes it has
# nothing to say. IBM's numbers are 55 for i, 50 for a and 53 by default, and
# they equalise rather than follow sonority -- a high vowel radiates less and
# is given more. 55 and 54 put the two open vowels inside the band its own
# five occupy, measured on tepa, tipa, tapa, topa and tupa against tepa and
# topa with a grave: 0.218 and 0.223 where Castilian's five run 0.192 to
# 0.223. The contrast Catalan needs is in the formants, not the loudness.
rule cat_ph_eopen_vals takes 1 from ss_ssval.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2722 to 55
  set global half 2930 to 600
  set global half 2938 to 1750
  set global half 2942 to 1750
  set global half 2946 to 2600
  set global half 2950 to 2600
  match
end

rule cat_ph_oopen_vals takes 1 from ss_ssval.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  set global half 2722 to 54
  set global half 2930 to 580
  set global half 2938 to 1000
  set global half 2942 to 1000
  set global half 2946 to 2500
  set global half 2950 to 2500
  match
end

# The vowel chain, with an eighth arm and the reduction in it.
#
# Central Catalan neutralises every unstressed a and e to the schwa and every
# unstressed o to u. That is not an accent, it is the vowel system: casa and
# casi differ in the first vowel and not the last, and a speaker who says the
# last one as a is not speaking Catalan. So the three arms ask the phone
# whether it carries stress and hand it to a different rule when it does not.
#
# It is done here rather than in the letter rules because stress is not known
# when a letter is read: the syllables have not been counted and the accent
# has not been placed. By the time the value chain runs, both have.
rule stanspan_vals takes 1 from ss_ssval.obj
  call ZZfence_null
  plant test try_e
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring113                      # i
    if answer is 0
      call stanspan_ph_i
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_e
  plant test try_a
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring114                      # e
    if answer is 0
      call cat_unstressed
      if answer is 0
        call cat_ph_schwa_vals
        go to tail
      end
      call stanspan_ph_e
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_a
  plant test try_u
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring115                      # a
    if answer is 0
      call cat_unstressed
      if answer is 0
        call cat_ph_schwa_vals
        go to tail
      end
      call stanspan_ph_a
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_u
  plant test try_o
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring117                      # u
    if answer is 0
      call stanspan_ph_u
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_o
  plant test try_schwa
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring116                      # o
    if answer is 0
      call cat_unstressed
      if answer is 0
        call stanspan_ph_u
        go to tail
      end
      call stanspan_ph_o
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_schwa
  plant test try_eopen
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call cat_test_schwa                                       # the schwa
    if answer is 0
      call cat_ph_schwa_vals
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_eopen
  plant test try_oopen
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call cat_test_eopen                                       # the open e
    if answer is 0
      call cat_ph_eopen_vals
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_oopen
  plant test try_w
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call cat_test_oopen                                       # the open o
    if answer is 0
      call cat_ph_oopen_vals
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_w
  plant test try_y
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring112                      # w
    if answer is 0
      call stanspan_ph_w
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place try_y
  plant test tail
  call ZZlpta_load_vvg__setscan_0103r__4
  if answer is 0
    call ZZtest_string_s_4_1_ZZstring108                      # y
    if answer is 0
      call stanspan_ph_y
      go to tail
    end
  end
  backtrack
place tail
  call cat_fem_breathiness
  call ZZstarttest16
  call nasalize_vow
  call ZZstarttest17
  call insert_acoustic_vals
  call succeed
  answer 0
end
